I serve as a technical mentor to Marvel’s React developers as we build full-stack capability across the team. Delivering a feature today often requires coordination between a UI developer and one of our .NET API developers. I help UI colleagues build on their React experience by tutoring them in API design, backend architecture, .NET development, and how our services run in Kubernetes.

I focus on helping colleagues understand the decisions behind the code. That includes how to define an API contract that meets the UI’s needs, decide where business logic belongs, and understand how a backend change moves from development to deployment. This gives UI developers a path to take on backend work with support and build the skills to own more of a feature end to end. Over time, the goal is to share delivery responsibility across a broader group of engineers and give our backend specialists more colleagues they can work with on API changes.
